## English (20 October 2026)

Subject: Unreal Engine Trainer (Nov 16 to Dec 4, 2026) : Matthieu Huguet, Technical Artist

Hello ProjProd team,

I am writing about your search for an Unreal Engine professional to lead your video game development training session from November 16 to December 4, 2026.

I really enjoyed Stéphane Biava's Unreal Engine courses and YouTube videos on @ProjProd: their clarity and practical approach to production workflows are what made me want to reach out directly.

My name is Matthieu Huguet, I am 25 and I work as a freelance Technical Artist, based in Aix-en-Provence, France.

I studied a Game Design Bachelor at LISAA Paris, a Master's at ARTFX Montpellier, then technical art courses at Gnomon and through Harvard CS50, before going freelance in early 2025.

In production, I worked as a freelance Technical Artist with Meerkat Studio on three simulation titles: Santa Simulator (shipped on Steam), Bakery Coffee Simulator (shipped on Steam), and Pet Grooming Simulator (paid contract). Earlier in my studies, I co-developed Noyes (student game). I also completed an archviz lighting project for a private client in Aix-en-Provence. All my work can be seen at matthieuhuguet.com.

Right now I am working on integrating and building solutions with Houdini and Unreal that generate level design through HDAs and let me iterate on it quickly. My latest published work: Fleur de Lys, Procedural Lily, Ceramic Tiles and HDA Stairs Component.

Your training program lines up directly with my daily practice and my Game Design and Technical Art background:
- Blueprint Visual Scripting, game logic, interactive systems and rapid gameplay prototyping.
- Level design, modular workflows and interactive environments.
- Real-time rendering (Lumen, PBR shaders, lighting) and performance optimization in Unreal Engine 5.

I truly enjoy breaking down technical concepts into clear, structured workflows for students and fellow artists, and I am fully comfortable teaching the entire session in English.

I am very open to short-term missions, available for the full window from November 16 to December 4, 2026, and can invoice directly as a freelancer.

I would be happy to talk with you by phone or video call, whenever suits you.

Matthieu Huguet

